-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, Subchapter IX -- LAYER 1, section 252:
-- the merger or consolidation of corporations of this State with foreign corporations; service of process on the
-- surviving or resulting corporation.
--
-- The source is lines 1058 to 1171 of de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script.
-- It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE (plain inputs, listed in NOTES.md): section 103 (dg1); section 155 (dg3); section 262 (dg7: only as the
-- appraisal proceeding that subsection (d) mentions); section 391(a)(29) (dg11: the fee); the laws of the other jurisdictions
-- (whether they prohibit the merger, how a foreign constituent corporation adopts the agreement, what they require it to state).
--
-- Section 252 applies to a merger of a corporation of this State with a FOREIGN corporation (section 371(a): a corporation
-- organized under the laws of any jurisdiction other than this State). The core's Entity says where an entity is formed.

§ `s 252 -- merger or consolidation of domestic and foreign corporations`

§§ `s 252(a) the power to merge or consolidate with a foreign corporation`

-- Plain gloss: one or more corporations of this State may merge or consolidate with one or more foreign corporations unless the
-- law of a foreign corporation's jurisdiction prohibits it, under an agreement that complies with, and is approved under, the
-- section. The resulting corporation of a consolidation "may be a corporation of the jurisdiction of organization of any 1 of the
-- constituent corporations".
-- src:1112 | Any 1 or more corporations of this State may merge or consolidate with 1 or more foreign corporations, unless the laws of the jurisdiction or jurisdictions under which such foreign corporation or corporations are organized prohibit such merger or consolidation. The constituent corporations may merge into a single surviving corporation, which may be any 1 of the constituent corporations, or they may consolidate into a new resulting corporation formed by the consolidation, which may be a corporation of the jurisdiction of organization of any 1 of the constituent corporations, pursuant to an agreement of merger or consolidation, as the case may be, complying and approved in accordance with this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 252(a) (src:1112)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 251 Kind of combination`
      `the number of constituent corporations that are corporations of this State` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of constituent corporations that are foreign corporations`        IS A NUMBER
      `the laws of the jurisdiction under which a foreign constituent corporation is organized prohibit the merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the laws of the other jurisdictions
      `the surviving corporation is one of the constituent corporations`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resulting corporation is a corporation of the jurisdiction of organization of one of the constituent corporations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement complies with s 252`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is approved in accordance with s 252`                          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 252(a) a corporation of this State may merge or consolidate with a foreign corporation` kind `the number of constituent corporations that are corporations of this State` `the number of constituent corporations that are foreign corporations` `the laws of the jurisdiction under which a foreign constituent corporation is organized prohibit the merger or consolidation` `the surviving corporation is one of the constituent corporations` `the resulting corporation is a corporation of the jurisdiction of organization of one of the constituent corporations` `the agreement complies with s 252` `the agreement is approved in accordance with s 252` MEANS
        `the number of constituent corporations that are corporations of this State` AT LEAST 1
    AND `the number of constituent corporations that are foreign corporations` AT LEAST 1
    AND (NOT `the laws of the jurisdiction under which a foreign constituent corporation is organized prohibit the merger or consolidation`)
    AND (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `a merger into a single surviving corporation`     THEN `the surviving corporation is one of the constituent corporations`
         WHEN `a consolidation into a new resulting corporation` THEN `the resulting corporation is a corporation of the jurisdiction of organization of one of the constituent corporations`)
    AND `the agreement complies with s 252`
    AND `the agreement is approved in accordance with s 252`

§§ `s 252(b) the agreement`

-- One field per limb of (b)(1) to (b)(7). (b)(3) is for a merger "in which the surviving corporation is a corporation of this
-- State", (b)(4) for a consolidation "in which the resulting corporation is a corporation of this State". (b)(7) is whatever the
-- laws of each foreign jurisdiction require the agreement to set forth (TRUE where they require nothing more).
-- src:1113 | (b) All the constituent corporations shall enter into an agreement of merger or consolidation. The agreement shall state:
-- src:1114 | (1) The terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation;
-- src:1115 | (2) The mode of carrying the same into effect;
-- src:1116 | In the case of a merger in which the surviving corporation is a corporation of this State, such amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation as are desired to be effected by the merger (which amendments or changes may amend and restate the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation in its entirety), or, if no such amendments or changes are desired, a statement that the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation shall be its certificate of incorporation;
-- src:1117 | (4) In the case of a consolidation in which the resulting corporation is a corporation of this State, that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as is set forth in an attachment to the agreement;
-- src:1118 | The manner, if any, of converting the shares of each of the constituent corporations into shares or other securities of the corporation surviving or resulting from the merger or consolidation, or of cancelling some or all of such shares, and, if any shares of any of the constituent corporations are not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into shares or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation or to be cancelled, the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity which the holders of such shares are to receive in exchange for, or upon conversion of, such shares and the surrender of any certificates evidencing them, which cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity may be in addition to or in lieu of the shares or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation;
-- src:1119 | Such other details or provisions as are deemed desirable, including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, a provision for the payment of cash in lieu of the issuance or recognition of fractional shares, rights or other securities of the surviving or resulting corporation or of any other corporation or entity the shares, rights or other securities of which are to be received in the merger or consolidation, or for some other arrangement with respect thereto, consistent with § 155 of this title; and
-- src:1120 | (7) Such other provisions or facts as shall be required to be set forth in an agreement of merger or consolidation (including any provision for amendment of the certificate of incorporation (or equivalent document) of a surviving or resulting foreign corporation) by the laws of each jurisdiction under which any of the foreign corporations are organized.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 252(b)(1) to (7) (src:1113-1120)
