-- The sentence defining "facts" in section 252(b): the same words as in section 251(b), read the same way (NOTES.md fork register F26): an
-- event, or a determination or action by any person or body (the corporation too), is a fact; anything else, the text does not say.
-- src:1121 | The term “facts,” as used in the preceding sentence, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 252(b) closing paragraph (src:1121)
GIVEN item IS A `s 251(b) Kind of item that a term may depend on`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 252(b) the item is a fact within the meaning of the closing paragraph` item MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `an event, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads`                                                         THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a determination or action by a person or body, including the corporation, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else, which the facts sentence of s 251(b) neither names nor excludes`                          THEN NOTHING

-- The agreement complies with the section when it states what (b) requires, any cash-in-lieu provision is consistent with
-- section 155, and -- if the surviving or resulting corporation is foreign -- it contains the agreement subsection (d) requires.
